hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16044","He said, Abd Allah narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Shaybah, he said, Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Yahya ibn al-Harith al-Taymi, from Yahya ibn Ghassan al-Taymi, from Ibn al-Rasim, from his father, that he said, we came as a delegation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he forbade us vessels. He said, then we came to him and said, our land is an unhealthy land. He said, so he said: Drink in whatever you wish, whoever wishes ties his waterskin upon sin."
"16045","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said, Abd al-Aziz ibn Muslim Abu Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abd Allah al-Taymi, from Yahya ibn Ghassan al-Taymi, from his father, he said, my father was among the delegation who came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from Abd al-Qays, and he forbade them these vessels. He said, so we became dyspeptic, then we came to him the next year. He said, so we said, O Messenger of Allah, you forbade us these vessels, and we became dyspeptic. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Make nabidh in whatever seems to you, and do not drink intoxicant, so whoever wishes ties his waterskin upon sin."
